INT. HOUSEBOAT GALLEY - THANKSGIVING - DUSK

A narrow kitchen the length of a railway carriage, every surface gleaming with small domestic order. Condensation clouds the porthole. Outside, lake water slaps the hull in the failing light. A turkey rests under foil on the counter, steaming faintly.

GRAN ODALYS BEAUCHAMP, seventy, sits at the end of the fold-down table with a crocheted shawl across her knees. Her daughter KEZIAH, forties, moves between stove and sink with the quick, precise gestures of someone who has done this a hundred times. Her husband PAVEL, forties, stands in the doorway with a bottle of wine, unsure where to put it, and at the table's other end EZRA, twelve, folds a paper napkin into a series of increasingly elaborate boats.

She says nothing. He says nothing. The kettle begins to whistle.

KEZIAH
(to the room)
Everyone sit. It's almost ready.

PAVEL
I'll pour.

KEZIAH
You'll pour after grace.

PAVEL
I can pour before grace.

She shoots him a look. He sets the bottle down and sits. Ezra's boat tips on its side. He rights it.

GRAN ODALYS
Ezra, darling. Come sit by me.

EZRA
I'm fine here.

GRAN ODALYS
Come sit by me.

He slides along the bench. She pats his knee. For a moment, nobody breathes, and the water laps and the kettle shrieks and Keziah moves it off the flame without looking.

KEZIAH
(muttering to herself)
Don't. Don't. Don't.

She carries the turkey to the table, slides it into place, and unwraps the foil. Steam rises over their faces. Pavel clears his throat.

PAVEL
It looks wonderful.

GRAN ODALYS
It looks like the one from nineteen eighty-eight.

KEZIAH
Mother.

GRAN ODALYS
I'm saying it's lovely.

She lifts her glass of water. Looks at each of them in turn. Her gaze stops on Keziah.

GRAN ODALYS (CONT'D)
(to everyone)
I have something to tell you all.

Ezra stops folding. Pavel sits very still. Keziah grips the carving knife.

GRAN ODALYS (CONT'D)
(to Keziah)
I sold the house.

KEZIAH
(a whisper)
Mother.

GRAN ODALYS
And I'm moving onto this boat.

Silence. The water slaps. The turkey steams. Ezra lets go of the napkin and it unfolds on the table.
